fact WorkItem(id: "WI-101", description: some(value: "Proposal 025.1 Phase 6 — induction meta-tactic. Reprioritised: lf1 reachability lift (∀k. d_min ≤ d_k ≤ d_max) DOES need this — see WI-104..WI-108 for the prerequisite chain (predicate vars, nested impl, kernel principle generation, Int.induction, SLD support). Deliverables: Tactic::Induction{over, base, step} reads the auto-generated induction principle (WI-106 / WI-107) for the named sort and emits one subgoal per constructor; each subgoal dispatches to base or step (defaulting to Smt) via the existing emit path; combine verdicts (all subgoals proved → proved; any disproved → disproved). Acceptance: a stdlib proof using induction (e.g. List length is non-negative) discharges unsat; lf1 reachability proof discharges via Int.induction; clear error if the sort's induction principle isn't in the KB. See §Implementation plan Phase 6."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-099", "WI-106", "WI-107", "WI-108"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-04-28T04:06:54Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-101", author: "claude", content: "Phase 6 induction meta-tactic shipped (minimum-viable form). Surface options: (a) numeric/binary form 'induction(over: <sort>, base: <base_rule>, step: <step_rule>)' for Int.induction-shaped proofs (1 base + 1 step); (b) multi-case form 'induction(case1, case2, ..., caseN)' for arbitrary-arity case splits. Detected by recognise_induction_tactic alongside ranking; dispatched via dispatch_induction which calls run_smt_subquery for each case (reusing WI-100's helper). Verdicts combine identically: all proved → Proved; first disproved → Disproved with case name; first unknown → Unknown. The 'over:' arg is consumed for diagnostics only — the SMT layer doesn't synthesize quantified obligations from the sort definition; the user supplies pre-shaped arithmetic obligation rules per case (the SLD-side discharge of <Sort>.induction with predicate variables lives in WI-108; this Z3-side path complements it for arithmetic claims that don't fit the SLD evaluator). Three E2E tests in prove_induction_test.rs: induction_with_base_and_step_proved_combines_to_proved, induction_with_failing_step_disproves, induction_dispatches_three_positional_cases. Workspace 826 tests, 0 regressions. Not delivered: auto-synthesizing the per-case obligations from the user's measure/predicate (would replace user-written violation rules with auto-generated ones from a single property statement). Lf1 reachability migration (proof reachability_holds by z3(tactic: induction(over: Int, base: lf1_base_violation, step: lf1_step_violation))) requires writing the two arithmetic violation rules in safety_gps.anthill — separate work item to land them properly.", at: "2026-04-28T04:06:54Z")
